150
00:07:07,288 --> 00:07:12,288
But no matter what I did, I wasn't as good as everyone else was.

151
00:07:12,288 --> 00:07:16,688
I hated how new kids would get so much better than me.

152
00:07:16,688 --> 00:07:21,088
My folks picked up on it fast, though, and let me quit right away.

153
00:07:21,088 --> 00:07:28,488
In fact, we had a whole tradition where they'd make my favorite food on the days I quit something.

154
00:07:28,488 --> 00:07:32,888
When I failed my exams, and when I hurt my nose.

155
00:07:32,888 --> 00:07:33,888
Your folks sound nice.

156
00:07:33,888 --> 00:07:34,888
Yep.

157
00:07:34,888 --> 00:07:38,888
Although, I'm a bit worried.

158
00:07:38,888 --> 00:07:39,888
Huh?

159
00:07:39,888 --> 00:07:44,888
I'm surrounded by so many great people.

160
00:07:44,888 --> 00:07:50,888
That's why I never realize when I'm being such a burden on them.

161
00:07:50,888 --> 00:07:59,688
At this rate, one day, I'm going to burden them too much, and then it's going to make them hate me.

162
00:07:59,688 --> 00:08:00,688
Yamada.

163
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:02,688
Ah, sorry.

164
00:08:02,688 --> 00:08:07,088
Look at me all teary-eyed.

165
00:08:07,088 --> 00:08:15,488
I don't know how your parents feel, but I think people would tell you when you're too much or when they've had enough.

166
00:08:15,488 --> 00:08:18,288
They'd be straight with you.

167
00:08:18,288 --> 00:08:20,088
I've said as much before.

168
00:08:20,088 --> 00:08:23,888
Hey, can I ask you something that's been on my mind for a bit?

169
00:08:23,888 --> 00:08:24,888
Huh?

170
00:08:24,888 --> 00:08:30,888
Back before winter break, there were two days you didn't come hang out in the library, remember?

171
00:08:30,888 --> 00:08:36,688
You said you had stuff to do, but did you really?

172
00:08:36,688 --> 00:08:39,688
I've been wondering.

173
00:08:39,688 --> 00:08:44,688
You said you could be straight and let me know when things are just too much for you.

174
00:08:44,688 --> 00:08:47,488
But I don't think you can.

175
00:08:47,488 --> 00:08:49,488
I mean, I know.

176
00:08:49,488 --> 00:08:52,488
I know you're way too nice to say something.

177
00:08:52,488 --> 00:08:54,488
It scares me.

178
00:08:54,488 --> 00:08:59,488
I'm so sorry about this.

179
00:08:59,488 --> 00:09:03,288
I know I must be such a pain.

180
00:09:03,288 --> 00:09:06,088
Wait.

181
00:09:06,088 --> 00:09:07,088
Wait.

182
00:09:15,088 --> 00:09:17,088
I'm sorry I lied.

183
00:09:17,088 --> 00:09:21,088
I just didn't have it in me.

184
00:09:21,088 --> 00:09:24,888
I didn't want to get hurt.

185
00:09:24,888 --> 00:09:27,888
So, of course, I closed myself off.

186
00:09:27,888 --> 00:09:30,888
I was just afraid she'd hate me.

187
00:09:34,888 --> 00:09:35,888
That's right.

188
00:09:35,888 --> 00:09:38,688
We're a bit alike.

189
00:09:38,688 --> 00:09:43,688
Napa cabbage is best when mushy.

190
00:09:43,688 --> 00:09:45,688
Don't fill it to the brim like that.

191
00:09:45,688 --> 00:09:46,688
Here.

192
00:09:46,688 --> 00:09:48,688
It's funny.

193
00:09:48,688 --> 00:09:50,688
I've been this exact way my whole life.

194
00:09:50,688 --> 00:09:54,688
So why am I suddenly worried about silly things like this now?

195
00:09:54,688 --> 00:09:59,688
I guess maybe...

196
00:09:59,688 --> 00:10:07,488
It's just because I...

197
00:10:07,488 --> 00:10:10,488
It could be because you've grown up.

198
00:10:10,488 --> 00:10:13,488
Grown-ups can get annoying.

199
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:14,488
You're right.

200
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:16,488
Guess that's true as well.

201
00:10:16,488 --> 00:10:18,488
Getting worried is a good thing.

202
